  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lupanda Beans Production and Marketing Expansion Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Agriculture - Beans.Beneficiaries: 168 small scale farmers, of which 91 are women.Lupanda Cooperative is a member owned cooperative that is located in Khosolo, Mzimba district. The members mainly grow beans for consumption and sale and maize for food security purposes. The cooperative has been implementing a USADF capacity building grant (EDI) and are requesting an expansion of the project. Under the EDI, the cooperative managed to increase its production from below 10 Metric Tons (MT) to 70MT by year 2. In addition, the cooperative now has basic financial and operation systems in place to better manage the cooperative and further increase production and eventually improve livelihoods.</narrative>
  </description>
